# Line-ending policy.
#
# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are executed INSIDE Linux containers. On a
# Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, git would otherwise rewrite their
# LF endings to CRLF; the `\r` then breaks /bin/sh ("syntax error: unexpected
# end of file") and any RUN step. Force these to LF in the working tree so the
# Docker build context is always correct, regardless of the host OS.
#
# (Root cause of the mcp-server `start.sh` crash — June 2026.)
*.sh         text eol=lf
Dockerfile*  text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf
entrypoint*  text eol=lf
